  "articlePanels": [
    {
      "kind": "lede",
      "html": "<p>You have decided to leave iAuditor. The hard part is doing it without losing your old Records. And without your team drifting back to paper. Here are five steps.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "takeaways",
      "heading": "The short version",
      "html": "<ul><li>Export every old Record before you cancel. PDF and CSV both come out of the SafetyCulture web dashboard.</li><li>Find which templates you really use. Skip the rest.</li><li>The biggest risk is people not using the new tool.</li><li>A tool with no new app and no new login removes that risk.</li><li>Try it with one or two people first. Then run both tools side by side.</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Why people leave",
      "heading": "It is use, not the product",
      "html": "<p>SafetyCulture (iAuditor) is a capable product. It has many templates and good reports. The trouble is use. Someone builds the templates. A few people use them. After a while the dashboard has far fewer Records than it should.</p><p>Then there is the bill. Each seat adds cost. A bigger team costs more, and the Records do not always follow.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Step 1",
      "heading": "Export before you cancel",
      "html": "<p>Do not cancel iAuditor until you have the Records you need. Once you close the account, access is gone.</p><p>In the SafetyCulture web dashboard, open Inspections. Filter by the templates you care about. Export as PDF or CSV. A large account takes time, so start early.</p><p>Templates export only in SafetyCulture's own format. Other tools cannot load them. But they show you the questions, so you can rebuild them. Most firms need two years of finished Records, plus the questions from the two or three templates in use.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Step 2",
      "heading": "Find what you really use",
      "html": "<p>Most people skip this step. It pays off most.</p><p>In SafetyCulture, look at the history for each template. Sort by last completed. Usually a few are recent. Many have not been touched in six months.</p><p>Do not move the unused ones. They only add clutter. Most firms need three to five.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Step 3",
      "heading": "Pick for how people work",
      "html": "<p>The common mistake is a better tool that people use just as little. Ask one question. What must a person do on day one? A download, an account, a password and a training session all risk people giving up.</p><p>Worth a look:</p><ul><li><strong>GoAudits</strong>: closest to iAuditor, lower price, app needed.</li><li><strong>Lumiform</strong>: European, simple, app needed.</li><li><strong>Paper and email</strong>: nothing to learn, but nobody can see it.</li><li><strong>Quickler</strong>: WhatsApp. No app. No login. You answer a message.</li></ul><p>Be honest about your team. If they like new systems, GoAudits or Lumiform may do. If people gave up on iAuditor, pick a tool that removes the barrier. See the <a href=\"/pages/iauditor-alternative-uk.html\">iAuditor alternative</a> page.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Step 4",
      "heading": "Bring the doubters along",
      "html": "<p>Some people resist any new system. That is fair. They have seen tools fail before.</p><p>Start with one or two people who are open to it. Run the new tool beside iAuditor for two to four weeks. Fix what they find. Then they can help the rest.</p><p>Listen to the doubts. They tell you what is wrong with the tool or the process. With WhatsApp there is nothing to install and no login to forget. The move is a message, not a training day.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "default",
      "eyebrow": "Step 5",
      "heading": "Run both. Do not cut hard.",
      "html": "<p>Do not cancel iAuditor on day one. Run both for four to six weeks. Your team has a fallback. Your Records have no gap.</p><p>Set a firm end date. Without one, the old tool never dies. At the end, export one last time. Close the account. Keep the export where you can find it for audits.</p><p>The checklist: export all Records as PDF and CSV. Export the templates you will move. Find the ones in use. Pick a tool people will use. Build the two to five that matter. Try it with one or two people for two to four weeks. Fix what they find. Set an end date. Export one last time. Cancel. Keep the confirmation. For the money side, see <a href=\"/pages/iauditor-cost-uk.html\">iAuditor cost UK</a>.</p>"
    },
    {
      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>How do I export my data from iAuditor?</h3><p>Export finished inspections as PDF or CSV from the SafetyCulture web dashboard. Templates export in their own format, one at a time. Do this before you cancel.</p><h3>How do I know which templates are used?</h3><p>Open the inspection history for each template. Sort by last completed. If nothing was done in 90 days, do not move it.</p><h3>How long does a switch take?</h3><p>For a small team, two to four weeks. List what is used. Build it in the new tool. Try it with one or two people. Then roll out.</p><h3>What is the biggest risk when switching?</h3><p>People stop using the new tool. If it needs a new app or a new login, some will go back to paper. Pick a tool that asks for nothing new.</p>"
